    "vocabulary_construction": "Union of the main corpus's top max_features tokens by frequency and every token appearing in the supplementary corpus (see build_vectorizer) \u2014 guarantees real-brand tokens survive regardless of how large the main corpus is. An earlier max_features-only approach passed this check at a 500k-row diagnostic scale but silently failed at the full ~4.5M-row scale (all sample brand tokens pruned, realistic-text accuracy back to 54%) \u2014 see ml/log.md.",
    "reason": "A stress test (see realistic_text_stress_test) measured only 50% accuracy on realistic text before this was added, because the main dataset's merchant names are template placeholders with no real brand-name overlap. This mixes in real vocabulary without diluting the main dataset's signal, by weighting rather than duplicating rows."
  },
